{"_id":"6a2ff9c82204ffbc59e5a7dd","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"zx7uCaQiCxvXMhm9FG3XG","description":"# Seaborn\n\nSeaborn is a Python visualization library built on Matplotlib that provides a higher-level interface for statistical graphics. It handles common plot types with less code and integrates tightly with Pandas DataFrames. Seaborn is particularly strong for visualizing statistical relationships, distributions, and grouped comparisons.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Seaborn Tutorials","url":"https://seaborn.pydata.org/tutorial.html","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb4d"},{"type":"official","title":"Introduction to Seaborn for dataviz with Python","url":"https://python-graph-gallery.com/seaborn/","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb4e"},{"type":"article","title":"Data Visualisation Tutorial Using Seaborn","url":"https://towardsdatascience.com/data-visualisation-tutorial-using-seaborn-26e1ef9043db/","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb4f"},{"type":"video","title":"Introduction to Seaborn","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vaf4ir8eT38&list=PLtPIclEQf-3cG31dxSMZ8KTcDG7zYng1j","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb50"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T13:10:32.508Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/zx7uCaQiCxvXMhm9FG3XG.md"}